+## E4 Per-line overflow hint
+
+- Status: done. Verdict: **not adopted** (rule failed: no speed gain, digest differs).
+- Design (before any reading): in the ghost table, a side array of 2-bit stamps, one per primary line of the main table (32 per word: lines/256 bytes). `ghost.add` sets the stamp of the history's primary line (`id >> 28`) to its newest slice (mod 3, + 1; the max with the stamp's live slice) before writing the entry or floor, committing only while the epoch it decoded against is current, as the entries do. `advance` clears dead stamps in the same sweep as the entries, so stamps decode unambiguously against the epoch (live slices are cur−2..cur). A read loads the epoch, the stamp, and the epoch again (retrying if it moved), and skips the overflow read when the stamp is 0 or its slice is dead at `now` over the horizon. ConstantTime always reads (its loads must not depend on the key).
+- Note written before measuring: a skipped read drops what the overflow table gives a key that never spilled: other keys' floors (to `Upper`) and fingerprint matches with other keys' entries (to `Count`, `Seen`, `Degraded`). `Upper` stays at or above the truth (the key's own histories always set its line's stamp first), but those answers change, so the digest may differ; the rule's "digest identical" is kept as written.
+- Rule (the experiment's, unchanged, before any reading): CountOverflowLive and TouchOverflowLive each faster (geomean < 0.59, interval < 1.00); no benchmark slower (CheckAndTouchOverflowLive, CheckAndTouchHit, TouchAndCount, InsertSteady, CheckAndTouchMissInsert not above 1.41 with the interval above 1.00); heavy16x Mops/s ≥ 1.10x HEAD's in at least 5 of 6 pairs; digest identical; `go test -race -count=3 -run '^TestGhost' .` passes. Void if a null arm leaves [0.59, 1.41]. Also reported: heavy4x pairs, Bytes() before and after, false denies.
