+- Status: done. Verdict: **not adopted** (rule failed: InsertSaturated 0.722 is not under 0.59; heavy16x ≥ 1.10x in 2 of 6 pairs).
+- Design (before any reading): reuse the filter-wide search-pressure EWMA (`f.pressure`, which moves 1/8 toward "fail" on every failed search and 1/8 toward "succeed" on every success). When it reads 15/16 or more (about 21 consecutive failures from a calm table), `claimAt` skips `warmAlts` and the relocation search and goes straight to the eviction choice, except for 1 in 16 inserts (by 4 fingerprint bits), which still search as probes; skipped inserts leave the pressure alone. A probe's success moves the pressure back below the threshold, so searching resumes after a success, including once a decay pass or expiry has freed slots. No new field; answers change only where the shortcut fires (saturated tables).
